          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On September 15, 2012, at approximately 1:35 PM, a witness is intrigued by the silent SSE-NNE movement of a elongated, colored object in the sky. As an amateur photographer, he reflexively takes two photographs. Due to a moderate southeast to east wind (see Meteociel report on Nice), the witness observes and photographs to the southeast a flying object with a complex shape, colored purple-blue. The object's movement appears consistent with the wind direction, and its appearance suggests a silver festive balloon (Mylar) inflated with helium. As the witness is facing into the wind on his balcony, he cannot accurately estimate the wind direction. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a festive balloon.",
